Awesome. Let's knock out **Bug 2: Broken Transaction Boundaries & Manual JDBC Connections**.
### The Problem
In JournalRequestServiceImpl, your processChunkRaw method bypasses Spring entirely to grab a raw connection and manually commit [cite: 764-775].
```java
// The dangerous part of your existing code:
try (Connection conn = dataSource.getConnection();
     PreparedStatement ps = conn.prepareStatement(sql)) {
     conn.setAutoCommit(false);
     // ...
     ps.executeBatch();
     conn.commit(); 
}

```
Because this runs inside the new ChunkWorker threads, it completely ignores the @Transactional wrapper of the parent method. [cite_start]Worse, if an exception occurs during conn.commit(), it throws a raw SQLException, bypassing Spring's DataAccessException translation. This can lead to connection leaks in HikariCP under heavy load and partial data corruption if the cleanup fallback doesn't catch the raw SQL error properly.
### The Fix
We will rewrite processChunkRaw to use Spring's jdbcTemplate.batchUpdate(). This allows Spring to manage the connection lifecycle, execute the batch efficiently, and translate any errors into standard DataAccessExceptions so your existing handleAsyncFailure rollback logic actually catches them.
Here is the code replacement.
